WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.262
This query demonstrates conditional aggregation with
CASE The grain is one row

00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:09.962
per subject_id so GROUP BY subject_id appears near
the end of the

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:14.825
statement Inside each patient group the first SUM
contains a CASE expression

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:20.075
that checks whether diagnosis equals Pneumonia
Matching rows contribute one while all

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.825
other rows contribute zero Adding those ones and
zeros gives the pneumonia

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:30.438
count The second SUM repeats the same idea for
Fracture This pattern

00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:34.588
may look unusual at first but it is very logical We
are

00:00:34.612 --> 00:00:39.200
converting a condition into numbers and then summing
the numbers One means

00:00:39.225 --> 00:00:43.325
this row belongs to the metric zero means it does
not Run

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:47.362
the query and inspect a few patient rows A patient
can have

00:00:47.388 --> 00:00:50.938
zero one or more admissions of each type depending
on the data

00:00:51.825 --> 00:00:55.012
CASE is especially useful when you need more than a
simple yes-or-no

00:00:55.038 --> 00:01:00.012
filter For example CASE can map categories to
different weights or values

00:01:00.038 --> 00:01:04.988
before aggregation For now focus on the pattern
condition one if true

00:01:05.213 --> 00:01:09.512
zero if false then SUM within the group That pattern
transfers to

00:01:09.525 --> 00:01:10.875
many SQL systems
